.!	MAN-PRELINK.RI		Man page for OOC Prelinker              Aug 89, bjw
.!
.!
.!
.! --------------
.!
.vs progname "prelink"
.vs product "Object Oriented C"
.!
.! --------------
.!
.source manual.rinc
.!
.! --------------
.!
.header /${progname}(OOPS)//${vers}/
.footer /%//Page #/
.!
.! +++++++++++++++++++++++++
.!
.section Name
${progname} - Invokes prelinker for O.O.C. Translator
.!
.! +++++++++++++++++++++++++
.!
.section Syntax
.bold
${progname}
C__outfile M__infile.. otherfiles..
.!
.! +++++++++++++++++++++++++
.!
.section Description
.!
Invokes the prelinker for the ${product} system.
The output file
.filename listfile
is created with a list of pointers to classes required
to build the final application.
The list is used to ensure the needed classes are
extracted from the ${product} libraries.
.sp
.!
The inputs to
.program ${progname}
are the class filenames and other files using message-expressions
created by the user for their application.
A list is built of all the classes and all their superclasses.
.sp
.!
The output
.filename listfile
must be passed to the C compiler, and then included during
the link phase.
This will cause the linker to extract the proper classes
from the library.
And then when the application starts running,
the substrate has a list of all the classes so they can be initialized.
For an example, see oct(OOPS)
.sp
.!
The are no options.
.!
.! +++++++++++++++++++++++++
.!
.section Diagnostics
If the "must init" file can't be located, awarning message is displayed.
.!
.! +++++++++++++++++++++++++
.!
.section Files
AMIGA: ooc:include/mustinit.ooc
.br
UNIX:  /usr/local/include/mustinit.ooc
.!
.! +++++++++++++++++++++++++
.!
.section See Also
cc(CP), oct(OOPS)
.br
.!
.!  *** EOJ
